{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14491 - MONDO_1239",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Fumarate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Anemia Of Prematurity through a series of mechanistic links. The evidence suggests that Ferrous Fumarate is associated with the treatment of deficiency anemias, including Iron Deficiency Anemia and Hypochromic Anemia, which are both linked to Anemia Of Prematurity. These relationships are supported by clinical indications and pharmacological pathways, indicating that Ferrous Fumarate may play a role in the management of anemia in preterm infants. The observed scores suggest a strong, though not absolute, association between Ferrous Fumarate and the development or management of Anemia Of Prematurity, likely through its effect on iron metabolism and hemoglobin synthesis. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential of Ferrous Fumarate as a therapeutic agent in the context of anemia in preterm infants, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm its direct role in the pathophysiology of this condition.",
